From eb7f815802126f817519473ba27ea97b156b663b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: James Dumay <jameswdumay@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 14:55:14 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(models): include <algorithm> in clef.cpp for MinGW builds

clef_get_spans() calls std::find() but the file only includes <cmath>, so the
call resolves through a transitive include. MinGW's libstdc++ does not provide
that path: the Windows Vulkan native runtime, which is the one Windows build
compiled with MinGW rather than MSVC, fails with

  src/models/clef.cpp:165:54: error: 'find' is not a member of 'std';
  did you mean 'bind'?

Include <algorithm> directly. The failure only shows up on a cold compile of
this file, which is why cached Windows backends never reported it.
---
 src/models/clef.cpp | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/models/clef.cpp b/src/models/clef.cpp
index cd2889b22..6f8720913 100644
--- a/src/models/clef.cpp
+++ b/src/models/clef.cpp
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@
 
 #include "llama-ext.h"
 
+#include <algorithm>
 #include <cmath>
 
 void llama_model_clef::load_arch_hparams(llama_model_loader & ml) {
